             :plan "`seon.render.value/show` with `:seon.render/outputs #{:hiccup}` throws `seon.instrument/contract-error` from `seon.ai.tokens/estimate` (argument `text` is nil, called from show's `answered`) on a value whose root render fails, while the same request with both outputs answers. Reproduce on default (JVM mode, the request `seon.printer-baseline/unit` builds) with the pinned sample `seon.ai/attempt#0` of `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-16/render-bench/samples.edn`, `(seon.render.value/show (assoc request :seon.render/output :seon.render/html :seon.render/outputs #{:hiccup}))`; three samples throw (`seon.ai/attempt#0`, `seon.db.write/entity-refusal#0`, `seon.test.accretion/install-refused-error#0`, rows in `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-16/render-bench/results/7d74a762f.edn`). Fix at the producer: `show` computes `:seon.render.value/tokens` from the answer's own text member, so the token charge must come from the tree it emitted whatever outputs are asked for, never from a member the output set may have dropped. Proof: a row in a table test over the three outputs sets (`#{:text}`, `#{:hiccup}`, both) on a value whose root render fails, answering a map with `:seon.render.value/tokens` and the diagnostic in each. Read `seon.render.value/show` and `seon.render.value-test`."}
